{
  "scenario_spec_version": 1,
  "scenario_id": "prototype_pump_validation",
  "title": "Prototype Pump: Validation and Activation",
  "description": "Ari is the validation engineer, Mara the coordinator, and Bo operates a prototype pump. The scenario concerns whether it is safe to activate. The pump initially fails validation. Ari alone knows that sensor channel C drifted 8 units in validation batch V17. Mara knows the public procedure and has received a short report stating that validation failed, without the private channel or batch detail. Bo knows the public procedure and has received no failure report. Under the public procedure, filing a validation hold reveals failed validation but not private test details. A false warning cannot change the pump's actual condition. Completing a review or waiting does not repair it. Ari may perform an explicit technical repair and authorized revalidation. Passing revalidation clears only the technical hold; activation also requires Mara's and Bo's separate recorded assents.",
